From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 18 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: libipa: add a camera sensor helper for the OV5648

The PineTab 2 rear camera is an OV5648, which has no helper, so the software
ISP logs

  IPASoft: Failed to create camera sensor helper for ov5648

and falls back to treating the raw V4L2_CID_ANALOGUE_GAIN code as a gain
multiplier. The sensor's gain registers hold a 10-bit value in 1/16 steps,
the same scaling the OV5647 uses, so AEGC converges on badly wrong gains
without it.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
diff -ruN lc_a/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp lc_b/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
--- a/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp	2026-09-18 06:47:45.682675565 +0200
+++ b/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp	2026-09-18 06:47:45.710207144 +0200
@@ -748,6 +748,21 @@
 };
 REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("ov5647", CameraSensorHelperOv5647)
 
+class CameraSensorHelperOv5648 : public CameraSensorHelper
+{
+public:
+	CameraSensorHelperOv5648()
+	{
+		/*
+		 * The gain registers (0x350a/0x350b) hold a 10-bit value in
+		 * 1/16 steps, so 0x0010 is unity gain. The sensor applies its
+		 * own black level correction, so no blackLevel_ is needed.
+		 */
+		gain_ = AnalogueGainLinear{ 1, 0, 0, 16 };
+	}
+};
+REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("ov5648", CameraSensorHelperOv5648)
+
 class CameraSensorHelperOv5670 : public CameraSensorHelper
 {
 public:
